      "math_academy_id": "q-78565",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Consider a matrix equation $B\\,x=A\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $2\\times 2$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $B$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${B}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $B\\,x=A\\,d$ by ${B}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}B\\,x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d \\\\ {I}_{2}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d \\\\ x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
